// SUBRT.QS0 - reusable subcircuits via GATE/ENDGATE and CALL.
//
// Demonstrates: the subroutine feature.
//
// Qubit-level explanation:
//   A GATE block defines a named subcircuit whose body operates on formal
//   parameters (qubits 0..nparams-1 inside the body). A call binds real
//   qubits to those parameters, positionally. Bodies are stored once in a
//   separate program region and reached by jump-based calls, so no code is
//   duplicated.
//
//   Here "bell 2" creates a Bell pair on its two arguments. Calling it twice,
//   on (0,1) and (2,3), builds two independent Bell pairs:
//       (|00>+|11>)/sqrt2  tensor  (|00>+|11>)/sqrt2
//     = (|0000>+|0011>+|1100>+|1111>)/2.
//   The four outcomes are each measured with probability 1/4. Because the
//   circuit is composed from one primitive, editing the GATE body updates
//   every call site at once.
//
// Run:
//   plasma run examples/SUBRT.QS0 --shots 1000
//   plasma run examples/SUBRT.QS0 --gpu --shots 1000
QUBITS 4
GATE bell 2
H 0
CNOT 0 1
ENDGATE
bell 0 1
bell 2 3
SHOT 1000
PRINT
END